From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Keitel <jkeitel@google.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:36:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/48] Use base::WeakPtr for callbacks in address save/update
 views

Since the view owns the controller and destroys the controller on
hide, there is a brief period in which the callbacks bound to the
view come dangling. In practice, this does not matter since the
view disappears synchronously (even if the widget is destroyed
async) and base::Unretained uses raw_ptr, but this seems cleaner.

The CL also removes an unnecessary GetTitle method since the title
is already set in the constructor.

Bug: 566935544
Change-Id: Ie1ea7daca629d6d7ab560a6232ebfd6e317fbdc9
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8467990
Reviewed-by: Bruno Braga <brunobraga@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Jan Keitel <jkeitel@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706861}
(cherry picked from commit db2e7db91c469b9a9073be105dd4f5919c1ed1f5)
